<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
  <!--
    Day half of the DayNight pair; `values-night/themes.xml` carries the night half. The window
    background has to follow the system setting on its own, because it is painted before the first
    Compose frame - a light window under a dark `StarterTheme` is a white flash on every launch.

    The platform's own DayNight parents start at API 29 while this template's minSdk is 26, and
    pulling in AppCompat or the Material Components library only to inherit a theme parent would
    add a dependency the app does not otherwise use. The `-night` resource qualifier is the same
    mechanism with nothing extra on the classpath.

    System bars are deliberately not styled here: `MainActivity` calls `enableEdgeToEdge()`, which
    owns bar transparency and icon contrast, and a theme attribute would fight it.
  -->
  <style name="Theme.KMPComposeStarter" parent="android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar" />
</resources>
